{"id":20811,"title":"Neural Radiance Fields in 3D Vision: A Comprehensive Review","url":"https://doi.org/10.26599/cvm.2026.9450535","final_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2210.00379","year":2026,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.26599/cvm.2026.9450535","arxiv":null,"sha256":"f7aa690e6bbe009499a6af1c1e5c1beca7c325935e6b6dbab3b07ebada233ecf","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"upgrade:unpaywall","fetched_at":1793226959.5634348,"text_chars":229411,"abstract":"In March 2020, Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) revolutionized Computer Vision, allowing for implicit, neural network-based scene representation and novel view synthesis. NeRF models have found diverse applications in robotics, urban mapping, autonomous navigation, virtual reality/augmented reality, and more. In August 2023, Gaussian Splatting, a direct competitor to the NeRF-based framework, was proposed, gaining tremendous momentum and overtaking NeRF-based research in terms of interest as the dominant framework for novel view synthesis. We present a comprehensive survey of NeRF papers from the past five years (2020-2025). These include papers from the pre-Gaussian Splatting era, where NeRF dominated the field for novel view synthesis and 3D implicit and hybrid representation neural field learning. We also include works from the post-Gaussian Splatting era where NeRF and implicit/hybrid neural fields found more niche applications. Our survey is organized into architecture and application-based taxonomies in the pre-Gaussian Splatting era, as well as a categorization of active research areas for NeRF, neural field, and implicit/hybrid neural representation methods. We provide an introduction to the theory of NeRF and its training via differentiable volume rendering. We also present a benchmark comparison of the performance and speed of classical NeRF, implicit and hybrid neural representation, and neural field models, and an overview of key datasets.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://arxiv.org/pdf/2210.00379","https://doi.org/10.26599/cvm.2026.9450535","https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/11522668","https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11522668"],"cited_by":[{"path":"970-tensor-approximation.md","name":"Tensor Approximation","k":24},{"path":"1576-ray-marching-reference-min-max-octree.md","name":"Ray-marching Reference (Min-Max Octree)","k":6},{"path":"946-gaussian-splatting.md","name":"Gaussian Splatting","k":4},{"path":"970-nerf-training-loop.md","name":"NeRF Training Loop","k":24},{"path":"3409-mip-nerf-optimization-and-activation-details.md","name":"Mip-NeRF Optimization and Activation Details","k":3},{"path":"5124-nerf-rendering-alpha-compositing.md","name":"NeRF Rendering (Alpha Compositing)","k":1},{"path":"5083-hybrid-view-dependent-color-modeling.md","name":"Hybrid View-dependent Color Modeling","k":6},{"path":"3306-mip-nerf-360.md","name":"Mip-NeRF 360","k":3},{"path":"3406-coarse-to-fine-nerf.md","name":"Coarse-to-Fine NeRF","k":2},{"path":"1359-plenoctree-conversion.md","name":"PlenOctree Conversion","k":3},{"path":"1185-nerf-neural-radiance-fields.md","name":"NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields)","k":5},{"path":"3026-tensorf.md","name":"TensoRF","k":1},{"path":"1576-neural-volume-rendering.md","name":"Neural volume rendering","k":6},{"path":"10-neural-and-primitive-based-representations.md","name":"Neural and primitive-based representations","k":7},{"path":"44-radiance-field-optimization.md","name":"Radiance-field optimization","k":9},{"path":"5498-lpips-computation.md","name":"LPIPS Computation","k":1},{"path":"6198-nerf.md","name":"NeRF++","k":1},{"path":"7440-plenoxels.md","name":"Plenoxels","k":1},{"path":"6060-neus.md","name":"NeuS","k":3},{"path":"8117-diffusion-based-guidance-for-radiance-field-optimization.md","name":"Diffusion-Based Guidance for Radiance Field Optimization","k":5},{"path":"8582-regnerf.md","name":"RegNeRF","k":1},{"path":"8687-depth-supervised-nerf.md","name":"Depth-Supervised NeRF","k":2},{"path":"8660-d-nerf.md","name"